      "skos:prefLabel": "AlphaZero",
      "skos:definition": "A game-playing system from DeepMind that learned chess, shogi and Go from the rules alone by reinforcement learning through self-play, combining a deep neural network with Monte Carlo tree search; announced in December 2017 and published in Science in December 2018 after it defeated Stockfish in a 1,000-game match.",
