      "@type": "kto:Algorithm",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Bitboards",
      "skos:definition": "A board representation used by chess engines in which a set of squares is stored as one 64-bit integer, one bit per square, so that questions about many squares at once (occupancy, attacks, pawn pushes) are answered with a few bitwise machine instructions.",
