      "skos:prefLabel": "NNUE",
      "skos:definition": "An efficiently updatable neural network: a small, integer-quantized evaluation network with sparse inputs whose first layer is updated incrementally after each move, invented for computer shogi by Yu Nasu and adopted by Stockfish in 2020 to replace hand-written evaluation inside alpha-beta search.",
