      "@id": "kt:romantic-era",
      "@type": "kto:School",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Romantic era",
      "skos:definition": "The style that dominated master chess in the mid-to-late nineteenth century, built on rapid development, opening gambits and sacrificial attacks on the enemy king, whose leading figure was Adolf Anderssen and which gave way to Wilhelm Steinitz's positional, scientific approach.",
