      "@id": "kt:shatranj",
      "@type": "kto:Variant",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Shatranj",
      "skos:definition": "The Persian and Arabic form of chess, adopted from the Sasanian game chatrang after the 7th-century Arab conquest of Persia, played with a short-range counsellor and a leaping elephant; it was the game that reached Europe and remained standard there until the late 15th-century rule changes created modern chess.",
