      "@id": "kt:soviet-chess-school",
      "@type": "kto:School",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Soviet chess school",
      "skos:definition": "The state-backed chess culture and style of play that grew up in the USSR from the 1920s, led in practice and method by Mikhail Botvinnik, which prized the initiative, dynamic and unbalanced positions and deep systematic preparation, and whose players dominated the world championship from 1948 to 1972.",
