      "@id": "kt:bishop-pair",
      "@type": "kto:StrategicConcept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Bishop pair",
      "skos:definition": "The possession of both bishops when the opponent has given up one or both of theirs for a knight; because the two bishops together cover squares of both colours, the pair is usually reckoned a lasting advantage worth roughly half a pawn, growing as the position opens and pawns come off.",
