      "@type": "kto:StrategicConcept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Prophylaxis",
      "skos:definition": "The strategy of anticipating what the opponent wants to do and preventing it before it can be carried out; set out as a principle by Aron Nimzowitsch and later associated above all with Tigran Petrosian and Anatoly Karpov.",
