      "skos:prefLabel": "Evans Gambit",
      "skos:definition": "A gambit line of the Italian Game, 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Bc5 4.b4, in which White offers a wing pawn to gain time for c2-c3 and d2-d4, rapid development and an attack on the black king; devised by Captain William Davies Evans in the 1820s and never refuted.",
