      "skos:prefLabel": "Adolf Anderssen",
      "skos:definition": "German master and mathematics teacher from Breslau (1818–1879), winner of London 1851, the first international tournament, and of London 1862 and Baden-Baden 1870; the leading attacking player of the Romantic era, remembered for the Immortal and Evergreen games and for his losses in matches to Morphy (1858) and Steinitz (1866).",
      "kto:domain": "players",
      "dcterms:created": "2026-11-12",
