    {
      "@id": "kt:wilhelm-steinitz",
      "@type": "kto:Player",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Wilhelm Steinitz",
      "skos:definition": "Prague-born master (1836–1900) who became the first official world chess champion by beating Johannes Zukertort in 1886, held the title until losing to Emanuel Lasker in 1894, and laid the foundations of positional play with his theory of balance and the accumulation of small advantages.",
