      "skos:prefLabel": "Algebraic notation",
      "skos:definition": "The system for recording chess moves in which each square is named by a file letter (a–h) and a rank number (1–8) from White's side, and a move is written as the piece letter plus the destination square; FIDE recognises it as the only notation for its own events.",
