      "@id": "kt:fifty-move-rule",
      "@type": "kto:Rule",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Fifty-move rule",
      "skos:definition": "The FIDE rule that the player on the move may claim a draw once each side has made 50 consecutive moves without a pawn move or a capture; since 2014 FIDE also ends such a game automatically after 75 moves by each side.",
