    {
      "@id": "kt:candidate-moves",
      "@type": "kto:Technique",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Candidate moves",
      "skos:definition": "The short list of moves a player decides are worth examining before calculating any of them; popularised by Alexander Kotov as the first step of a disciplined search, and studied by psychologists who found that strong players examine few first moves but choose them well.",
