    {
      "@id": "kt:starting-age",
      "@type": "kto:CognitiveConcept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Starting age",
      "skos:definition": "The age at which a player first learns chess, begins serious study or joins a club, studied as a predictor of eventual playing strength; earlier starters reach higher ratings even when total practice is held constant, which some researchers read as evidence of a sensitive period.",
