      "skos:prefLabel": "Visualization",
      "skos:definition": "The ability to hold a chess position in mind and update it accurately as imagined moves are made, without moving the pieces; psychologists study it as the \"mind's eye\", a short-lived mental image that pattern recognition feeds and look-ahead search depends on.",
